673 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Six MRI brain scans with outlined red markings indicating specific areas of interest. Three scans are in the top row and three in the bottom row, each highlighting different regions with irregular red boundaries.) /K 735 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 221 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
674 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Diagram illustrating an encoder-decoder architecture for image processing. The encoder, starting with a STEM block, processes input through multiple LSC blocks across four stages, each increasing in complexity. The decoder reconstructs the output using BSC-Mamba blocks and trilinear interpolation, with data flow indicated by arrows. Feature maps and operations like batch normalization, convolution, and activation are part of the process. The layout incorporates various connection types, such as skip connections and up samples, to maintain data integrity.) /K 736 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 224 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
675 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Flowchart of a convolutional neural network architecture featuring two branches. Each branch starts with a 3D reshaping process. The first path involves a depthwise convolution followed by two 3D convolutions. The second path contains one 3D convolution and a depthwise convolution followed by another 3D convolution. Both paths merge, leading to batch normalization, another 3D convolution, and final output. Legend indicates "R" for reshape and "C" for convolution.) /K 737 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 224 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
676 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Diagram of a neural network architecture with labeled sections. The top section shows data flow through processes labeled "ASC," "Backward Scan," "Forward Scan," and "Mamba," with arrows indicating direction and operations like "Linear" and "De-flatten." The bottom section details the "ASC" process with components like "DWConv 3x3x3," "SE," "Conv3D," and "SeLU," leading to "DWConv 7x7x7." The right section highlights "Mamba" components such as "SSM," "Conv3D," and "Linear," with operations like "Deserialization," "Concatenation," and "Sigmoid" shown.) /K 738 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 225 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
677 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Diagram showing a neural network architecture with two parts. On the left, sequences D and E undergo 3D convolutions followed by depthwise convolutions, merging into Integration. On the right, D and E influence channel and spatial attention modules, followed by a softmax function and spatial attention, with results integrated through a 3D convolution.) /K 739 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 226 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
678 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Eleven images display the results of a medical image segmentation task using different models. The first image shows a brain scan with a highlighted red region labeled "Case." The other ten images display segmentation outputs in white on a black background, titled: Ours, Umamba, FRPnet, STU-Net, UNETR, Transunet, SwinUNet, U-Net++, and 3Dunet. The dataset is ATLAS 2.0.) /K 740 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 229 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
679 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Six line graphs compare LBMNet with different networks \(Umamba, FRPnet, UNETR, Transunet, SwinUNet, U-Net++\) by plotting Dice scores against lesion volume. Each graph shows LBMNet outperforming its counterpart as lesion volume increases.) /K 741 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 230 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
680 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Bland-Altman analysis comparing volume differences for small, medium, and large lesions across three panels. Each panel shows scattered data points with mean bias at -5.22% \(blue line\) and limits of agreement between 57.68% and -68.11% \(red lines\).) /K 742 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 231 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
681 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Medical imaging comparison showing a brain scan with a highlighted red area labeled "Case" and eight black images with small white regions labeled "Ours," "Uramamba," "FRPnet," "STU-Net," "UNETR," "Transunet," "SwinUNet," "U-Net++," and "3Dunet." Dataset is ISLES 2022.) /K 743 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 232 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
682 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Six brain MRI images labeled as "Case," "Model5," "Model4," "Model3," "Model2," and "Model1" are displayed in a two-row grid. Each image has a yellow-highlighted inset showing a zoomed-in portion with red and blue outlines, indicating areas of interest or abnormalities.) /K 744 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 233 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
683 0 obj
<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Line graphs comparing performance metrics. The left graph shows Dice Score percentages, increasing from 65.0% at Baseline to 68.0% at "Ours." The right graph displays IoU Score percentages, rising from 53.0% at Baseline to 55.5% at "Ours." Each graph indicates improvements across different models: Enc-Res, Enc-SA, Dec-CA, and "Ours.") /K 745 0 R /P 238 0 R /Pg 234 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
